 "_about": "Topkap\u0131: pale limestone for the gates, towers, walls and the ranges; white marble for the porticoes' columns and arcades, the Tower of Justice's lantern, the Baghdad and Revan kiosks and the terrace; Ottoman stone-and-brick (alma\u015f\u0131k) on the kitchens and the treasury; lead on every dome, cap and roof, the alems gilt, the Iftariye's canopy gilt; the painted soffits (sa\u00e7ak) under the porticoes and the kiosks' eaves; Iznik tiles inside the Divan and the Audience Chamber; the Sofa Kiosk's timber; the Mecidiye's white plaster; Hagia Irene's brick; the courts' lawns, paths and plane trees and cypresses.",
